\section{Anomaly Visualization}
\label{sec:anomaly_visualization}

This section describes the visual representation of the 3.55 keV spectral
anomaly and its spatial context within the Aether-Core/200LY simulation
volume.

\subsection{Spectral Profile Plot}
The spectral anomaly is visualized by plotting the differential intensity
$\Delta I(E)$:
\begin{equation}
\Delta I(E) = I_{\text{obs}}(E) - I_{\text{dec}}(E),
\end{equation}
over the relevant energy range.

\begin{figure}[h]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=0.8\textwidth]{figures/fig_anomaly_spectrum.png}
\caption{Differential spectral intensity $\Delta I(E)$ showing a
prominent peak at $E = 3.55 \; \text{keV}$.}
\label{fig:anomaly_spectrum}
\end{figure}

\subsection{Spatial Localization Map}
The spatial distribution of the anomaly is rendered as a 3D or projected
2D map of $\Delta I(\mathbf{x}, E = 3.55 \; \text{keV})$ across the
simulation domain.

\begin{figure}[h]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=0.8\textwidth]{figures/fig_anomaly_spatial.png}
\caption{Spatial map of anomaly intensity at $E = 3.55 \; \text{keV}$,
highlighting the localized feature at $(120, -45, 80)$ LY.}
\label{fig:anomaly_spatial}
\end{figure}

\subsection{Multi-Physics Overlay}
To illustrate the relationship between the anomaly and the surrounding
physical environment, the anomaly field is overlaid on MHD and N-body
structures.

\begin{figure}[h]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=0.8\textwidth]{figures/fig_anomaly_overlay.png}
\caption{Overlay of the 3.55 keV anomaly on density and magnetic field
structures, showing its position relative to local plasma and stellar
configurations.}
\label{fig:anomaly_overlay}
\end{figure}

\subsection{Temporal Stability Visualization}
Temporal persistence is visualized by plotting anomaly intensity over
simulation time:
\begin{equation}
I_{\text{anom}}(t) = \Delta I(\mathbf{x}_{\text{anom}}, E = 3.55 \; \text{keV}, t).
\end{equation}

\begin{figure}[h]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=0.8\textwidth]{figures/fig_anomaly_time.png}
\caption{Time series of anomaly intensity at the localized coordinates,
demonstrating stability across stress-test events and long-horizon
evolution.}
\label{fig:anomaly_time}
\end{figure}